+.. setting:: redis_backend_credential_provider
+
+``redis_backend_credential_provider``
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Default: Not configured
+
+The Redis backend supports credential providers as defined by
+``redis.CredentialProvider``. This value may be either a dotted path to a
+``redis.CredentialProvider`` subclass (which will be resolved and instantiated
+when the connection is set up) or an instance of such a class.
+
+When a credential provider is configured, the ``username`` and ``password``
+connection parameters are removed to avoid conflicts. Passing a value that is
+neither a valid dotted path to a ``redis.CredentialProvider`` subclass nor a
+``redis.CredentialProvider`` instance raises an error.
+
+The credential provider can also be supplied as a ``credential_provider``
+query parameter in the connection URL::
+
+    result_backend = 'redis://host:port/db?credential_provider=redis.CredentialProvider'
+
 .. setting:: redis_backend_use_ssl
 
